{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Gradient Clipping and Mixed Precision Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `clip_global_l2_norm` - a wrapper around `torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_` that returns both the pre-clip and post-clip norm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `has_non_finite_grad` - a helper that scans gradients for NaN and Inf."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `AmpTrainState` - wraps a model, an `AdamW` optimizer, a GradScaler, and an autocast device. Exposes a `step(inputs, targets)` that runs the full clipping, scaling, and skip-on-NaN pipeline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `StepLog` and `SkipLog` - structured per-step records."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that trains a small `nn.Linear` model for 20 steps, injects an Inf into the gradient on step 5 to exercise the skip path, and prints the resulting log."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The script exits zero and prints a per-step log with each row tagged `STEP` or `SKIP`; at least one row is a `SKIP`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Replace the synthetic Inf injection with a real loss spike (multiply one batch's target by 1e8) and verify the skip path triggers.\n2. Add a `--bf16` mode that switches autocast to BF16 instead of FP16. BF16 has a wider exponent range than FP16 and rarely needs loss scaling; verify the skip rate drops to zero on the same demo.\n3. Add a unit test that the gradient-clip wrapper returns the pre-clip and post-clip norm correctly when no clipping occurs.\n4. Add a rolling-window skip-rate computation and a CLI flag that fails the run if the rate exceeds a configured threshold for 100 consecutive steps.\n5. Wire the loop to write the canonical CSV (`step, lr, grad_l2_pre_clip, grad_l2_post_clip, loss, skipped, skip_reason, scaler_scale`) and confirm the file survives a Ctrl-C by flushing after every row."
      ]
    }
  ],
